{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-2200","published":"2026-05-09T11:11:11Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:19:51.018378164Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-43859","CVE-2026-43860","CVE-2026-43861","CVE-2026-43862","CVE-2026-43863","CVE-2026-43864"],"summary":"mutt security update","details":"Mutt is a small but very powerful text-based mail client for Unix operating systems.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nmutt before version 2.3.2 sometimes uses strfcpy instead of memcpy for the IMAP auth_cram MD5 digest, which may lead to buffer handling issues.(CVE-2026-43859)\n\nMutt email client before version 2.3.2 contains a vulnerability where the hash_passwd is sometimes truncated by one byte during IMAP auth_cram MD5 digest authentication, potentially causing authentication failures or security issues.(CVE-2026-43860)\n\nmutt before 2.3.2 does not check for &apos;\\0&apos; in url_pct_decode, resulting in improper null byte handling vulnerability.(CVE-2026-43861)\n\nIn mutt before version 2.3.2, the imap_auth_gss security level is mishandled, which may lead to security vulnerabilities.(CVE-2026-43862)\n\nmutt before 2.3.2 has an infinite loop in data_object_to_stream in crypt-gpgme.c.(CVE-2026-43863)\n\nmutt before version 2.3.2 has a NULL pointer dereference vulnerability in the show_sig_summary function.(CVE-2026-43864)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"mutt","ecosystem":"openEuler:22.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/mutt&distro=openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.2.12-4.oe2203sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["mutt-2.2.12-4.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","mutt-debuginfo-2.2.12-4.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","mutt-debugsource-2.2.12-4.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["mutt-help-2.2.12-4.oe2203sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["mutt-2.2.12-4.oe2203sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["mutt-2.2.12-4.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","mutt-debuginfo-2.2.12-4.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","mutt-debugsource-2.2.12-4.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"